{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01106",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.76,
      "end_seconds": 7.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "Okay, doctor, we're all set in here. I'll give you the numbers when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.08,
      "end_seconds": 12.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 13.48,
      "end_seconds": 17.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.77,
      "end_seconds": 24.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.81,
      "end_seconds": 32.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.72,
      "text": "Honestly, it's burning when I pass urine, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.51,
      "end_seconds": 34.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.02,
      "end_seconds": 42.46,
      "duration_seconds": 6.44,
      "text": "Erm, I'd say four weeks. Actually, no, closer to three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.83,
      "end_seconds": 49.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.33,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.78,
      "end_seconds": 56.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "It settles a little with drinking water. I'd say on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.95,
      "end_seconds": 64.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 64.54,
      "end_seconds": 71.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "Yeah, you know, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.29,
      "end_seconds": 85.94,
      "duration_seconds": 13.65,
      "text": "I was getting to that! Oh, and a dull ache low in my tummy. About dull ache low in my tummy, I'd say mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.48,
      "end_seconds": 91.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Any vaginal discharge, blood in the urine or back pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.33,
      "end_seconds": 109.02,
      "duration_seconds": 15.69,
      "text": "No, no vaginal discharge, no blood in the urine, no back pain. I was going to the toilet often at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.13,
      "end_seconds": 112.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Have you had any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.84,
      "end_seconds": 115.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Definitely no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 116.18,
      "end_seconds": 121.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.98,
      "end_seconds": 130.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.65,
      "end_seconds": 140.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.86,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.72,
      "end_seconds": 143.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.18,
      "end_seconds": 146.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.35,
      "end_seconds": 164.73,
      "duration_seconds": 11.38,
      "text": "I have about eight cigarettes in a day. I only drink at family occasions. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.93,
      "end_seconds": 169.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.28,
      "end_seconds": 175.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "Plasters. I come out in... well, a red itchy rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.95,
      "end_seconds": 180.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.57,
      "end_seconds": 191.82,
      "duration_seconds": 10.25,
      "text": "Asthma, for five years. I've had arthritis in my knees for five years now. I have low haemoglobin, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.48,
      "end_seconds": 196.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.07,
      "end_seconds": 205.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "It's Seretide inhaler, twice a day for my asthma. I take diclofenac, 50 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 207.48,
      "end_seconds": 216.9,
      "duration_seconds": 9.42,
      "text": "Um, doctor, I think the last prescription for the diclofenac was 25 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.72,
      "end_seconds": 221.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Alright. Did you bring the up-to-date prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.3,
      "end_seconds": 237.62,
      "duration_seconds": 15.32,
      "text": "No, you know, I left it at home. I take iron tablets, once a day. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I told my wife I'd come today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 250.8,
      "end_seconds": 262.73,
      "duration_seconds": 11.93,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. SpO2 98 percent on room air, respiratory rate 17, temp 36.5 degrees, blood pressure 110 over 81, pulse is 74 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.79,
      "end_seconds": 265.49,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.29,
      "end_seconds": 271.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.87,
      "end_seconds": 273.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.81,
      "end_seconds": 276.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.13,
      "end_seconds": 295.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft with slight tenderness just above the pubic bone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.98,
      "end_seconds": 300.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.44,
      "end_seconds": 350.78,
      "duration_seconds": 31.34,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, the most likely explanation is an uncomplicated urinary infection. Vaginal irritation is also on my list. You'll be taking nitrofurantoin, 100 milligrams, twice a day, three days. You take it by mouth. That's for urinary infection. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 351.61,
      "end_seconds": 357.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "That's fine by me. Can you send me for a urine dipstick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.95,
      "end_seconds": 369.41,
      "duration_seconds": 10.46,
      "text": "I don't think that's needed at this stage, the history doesn't call for it. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 370.31,
      "end_seconds": 373.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}